<BaseLayout title="Privacy | LiveDiscover"><section class="container page-section simple-page"><div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A little clarity</p><h1>Your night.<br/><i>Your privacy.</i></h1><p>How this demonstration website handles information.</p></div><div class="prose"><h2>Information stored on your device</h2><p>Saved events, followed artists, event submission drafts, and demo RSVP entries are stored in your browser’s localStorage. These entries stay on this browser and are not synced to an account or another device.</p><p>A draft may include the name, email address, and event details you enter. Demo RSVP entries include an email address and the number of guests. Avoid entering sensitive or private information into this demonstration.</p><h2>Forms and email</h2><p>This demo does not send event submissions or RSVP confirmations. The newsletter form cannot subscribe you until an email service is connected. It will display a message if delivery is unavailable.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>Venue maps load from OpenStreetMap when you scroll to them. Map providers receive the connection information normally sent by your browser. Direction links open Google Maps, and calendar links may open Google Calendar. Those services have their own privacy practices.</p><h2>Cookies and tracking</h2><p>No advertising or behavioral tracking scripts have been added to this demo. The hosting provider may keep operational request logs for serving and protecting the website.</p><h2>Clearing your information</h2><p>Clear this site’s storage in your browser settings to remove saved shows, follows, drafts, and demo RSVP records. Unsave individual shows with the heart button, or unfollow artists from their cards.</p><h2>Before a public launch</h2><p>The operator must update this notice with its identity, contact information, configured services, data retention periods, and applicable privacy requirements before accepting real submissions or reservations.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
